<article class="env-lemma" id="09QQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09QQ">Lemma <span data-tag="09QQ">22.27.9</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/09QJ" data-tag="09QJ">22.27.2</a> let $0 \to x \to y \to z \to 0$ be an admissible short exact sequence in $\text{Comp}(\mathcal{A})$. The triangle </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{x\ar[r] &  y\ar[r] &  z\ar[r]^{\delta } &  x[1]}  \]
</div>
  <p> with $\delta : z \to x[1]$ as defined in Lemma <a href="/tag/09P6" data-tag="09P6">22.27.1</a> is up to canonical isomorphism in $K(\mathcal{A})$, independent of the choices made in Lemma <a href="/tag/09P6" data-tag="09P6">22.27.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose $\delta $ is defined by the splitting 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ x \ar@<0.5ex>[r]^{a} &  y \ar@<0.5ex>[r]^ b\ar@<0.5ex>[l]^{\pi } &  z \ar@<0.5ex>[l]^ s }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       and $\delta '$ is defined by the splitting with $\pi ',s'$ in place of $\pi ,s$. Then 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  s'-s = (a\pi + sb)(s'-s) = a\pi s'  \]
</div>
    <p>
       since $bs' = bs = 1_ z$ and $\pi s = 0$. Similarly, 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \pi ' - \pi = (\pi ' - \pi )(a\pi + sb) = \pi 'sb  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Since $\delta = \pi d(s)$ and $\delta ' = \pi 'd(s')$ as constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/09P6" data-tag="09P6">22.27.1</a>, we may compute 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \delta ' = \pi 'd(s') = (\pi + \pi 'sb)d(s + a\pi s') = \delta + d(\pi s')  \]
</div>
    <p>
       using $\pi a = 1_ x$, $ba = 0$, and $\pi 'sbd(s') = \pi 'sba\pi d(s') = 0$ by formula (5) in Lemma <a href="/tag/09P6" data-tag="09P6">22.27.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>